# Trailing-slash canonicalization for static Astro pages.
# Astro emits /<path>/index.html and the sitemap lists the with-slash form.
# CF Pages serves matching static files BEFORE consulting these rules, so
# /themes/who-am-i/ still hits the Astro index.html unaffected. Without
# explicit 301s, the no-slash form (e.g. /themes/who-am-i) resolved via the
# SPA fallback below and rendered identical React content, creating
# duplicate-content entries in Google's index alongside the canonical URL.

# Pages that went when Agora became its stories. Each page also left the
# build, so these rules are what answers; both slash forms are listed, since
# no static file is left to normalize the slash, and they sit above the slug
# rules so the first matching rule is the final target (no chains). The
# figure list merged into the landing's list of the thirty.
/figures/      /#all        301
/figures       /#all        301
/de/figures/   /de/#alle    301
/de/figures    /de/#alle    301
/audio         /            301
/audio/        /            301
/de/audio      /de/         301
/de/audio/     /de/         301
/themes        /            301
/themes/       /            301
/themes/*      /            301
/de/themes     /de/         301
/de/themes/    /de/         301
/de/themes/*   /de/         301
/echoes        /methodology/ 301
/echoes/       /methodology/ 301
/de/echoes     /de/methodik/ 301
/de/echoes/    /de/methodik/ 301
/open-source-philosophy-app     /about/    301
/open-source-philosophy-app/    /about/    301
/de/open-source-philosophy-app  /de/about/ 301
/de/open-source-philosophy-app/ /de/about/ 301
/ai-philosophy-tutor            /          301
/ai-philosophy-tutor/           /          301
/talk-to-historical-figures     /          301
/talk-to-historical-figures/    /          301
/de/philosophie-lernen          /de/       301
/de/philosophie-lernen/         /de/       301

