# App SPA — the React app (login + in-app surface) lives under /app. The
# rewrite destination must be the NORMALIZED form /app/ — CF Pages 308s any
# /app/index.html request to /app/ at the asset layer, and a rewrite that
# targets the pre-normalization path falls through to the 404 page instead of
# serving the shell (observed live 2026-06-10 once 404.html existed). The
# asset layer also 308s bare /app → /app/ on its own, before these rules.
/app    /app/  200
/app/*  /app/  200

# No catch-all on purpose (removed 2026-06-10). The old `/* /app/index.html 200`
# answered every junk URL with a 200 SPA shell whose canonical pointed at the
# homepage, a classic soft-404 that erodes crawl trust. The SPA owns exactly
# /app and /app/* (rules above). Everything else either matches a static Astro
# file, a rule here, or gets the real 404.html, which CF Pages serves with
# HTTP status 404 whenever a root 404.html exists in the build.
